# Worker RUNTIME secrets, for `wrangler dev` and `npm run preview`.
# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# This file is NOT the same thing as `.env`. `.env` holds BUILD-time variables
# that Vite inlines while `astro build` runs. `.dev.vars` holds variables the
# Worker reads at REQUEST time through `cloudflare:workers`, which is the only
# place the live-preview stack can get a token: the preview routes are
# `prerender = false` and run per request, long after the build is over.
#
# In production these are set with:
#   npx wrangler secret put SANITY_TOKEN

# Sanity token with read access to DRAFT documents. Powers /preview/*,
# /preview/live and /api/draft-mode/enable. Without it those routes fail closed
# with a 503 naming what is missing, rather than quietly serving published
# content dressed up as a draft.
#
# Create at https://sanity.io/manage/project/ba403vjc/api/tokens with Viewer
# permission. It may be the same value as SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN in .env; the
# names are separate because the two live in different places and rotate
# independently.
#
# Rotating it invalidates every outstanding preview cookie (the cookie value is
# a fingerprint of this token, see src/lib/preview-auth.ts). Editors just reopen
# the Presentation tool.
SANITY_TOKEN=
